# The chrome's words are set in a face of the machine's, through the font
# stack, by what each glyph measures: the families the theme names. Run with
# --fonts builtin --add-font <build>/SashfoldTestSans.ttf and the theme beside
# this script, which names that face at 20 px: its letters are plain boxes,
# 14 px tall from the baseline, in cells of 5 px (f i j l r t), 18 px (m w)
# and 10 px (the rest), each box 1 px in from either side of its cell, and a
# middle letter before a wide one is kerned 2 px closer. Ink is #e6e8ec; the
# front tab #2c313a; the address field #14161b; the caret #5b9cf6. The
# built-in face's advance at this size is 12.5 px whatever the letter.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>mmmmmmmmmmmm</title><body style="margin:0">
assert-theme-problem none

# A tab's title, cut by what it measures and not by a count of its letters.
# The title starts at x 14 and has 182 px; twelve m are 216. With 12.5 px kept
# for the ellipsis nine fit (162 px): the ninth box is columns 159 to 174,
# rows 13 to 26, and where a tenth would stand there is the tab.
assert-pixel 165 13 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 165 12 #2c313a
assert-pixel 165 26 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 165 27 #2c313a
assert-pixel 185 14 #2c313a

# The address: its words start at x 123 on the baseline at y 62, so a box is
# rows 48 to 61. Four m are 72 px: the fourth box is columns 178 to 193, and
# the caret stands at 123 + 72 = 195 — not at 173, where four advances of the
# built-in face would put it.
key ctrl+l
type mmmm
assert-pixel 185 48 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 185 47 #14161b
assert-pixel 185 61 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 185 62 #14161b
assert-pixel 195 47 #5b9cf6
assert-pixel 173 47 #14161b

# A kerned pair is drawn as close as it is measured: a is 10 px, m starts
# 2 px sooner for it, so its box is columns 132 to 147 (not 134 to 149) and
# the caret after it stands at 123 + 26 = 149 (not 151).
key ctrl+l
type am
assert-pixel 132 49 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 148 49 #14161b
assert-pixel 149 47 #5b9cf6
assert-pixel 151 47 #14161b

# A narrow letter takes a narrow cell: r is 5 px, its box columns 124 to 126;
# then the m, columns 129 to 144; and the caret at 123 + 23 = 146.
key ctrl+l
type rm
assert-pixel 125 49 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 127 49 #14161b
assert-pixel 129 49 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 146 47 #5b9cf6

# The window's words are never a page's to dress: a page that brings a font
# along under the very name the chrome's face goes by — here the built-in
# face's own outlines — changes nothing above the page.
open data:text/html,<style>@font-face{font-family:"Sashfold Test Sans";src:url(data:font/ttf;base64,)}</style><body style="margin:0;font:40px 'Sashfold Test Sans'">ae
key ctrl+l
type mmmm
assert-pixel 185 48 #e6e8ec
assert-pixel 195 47 #5b9cf6
